   "onlineUrl": "https://doi.org/10.1111/bjh.70727",
   "overview": "Laboratory guidance for TTP, covering the whole pathway: spotting it on an FBC and film, turnaround times, sampling and pre-analytical handling, ADAMTS13 activity assays and how to interpret them (including the 10–20 IU/dL grey area and the HemosIL CLEIA caveat), anti-ADAMTS13 antibodies, antigen and conformation assays, monitoring in remission and relapse, EQA, and the consultant's role in supporting the laboratory. The central message is that treatment must never wait for the ADAMTS13 result.",
   "recommendations": [
    {
     "id": "recog-1",
     "group": "Laboratory investigation for TTP",
     "grade": "1C",
     "text": "Haematology laboratories should have documented processes in place to ensure that new patients with full blood count samples with thrombocytopenia, especially those with platelet count <30 × 10⁹/L, are examined microscopically for evidence of haemolysis.",
     "page": 2
    },
    {
     "id": "recog-2",
     "group": "Laboratory investigation for TTP",
     "grade": "1C",
     "text": "Haematology laboratories should have a documented process in place to ensure that new patients with blood films with thrombocytopenia and evidence of haemolysis are escalated rapidly for clinical review.",
     "page": 2
    },
    {
     "id": "tat-1",
     "group": "Turnaround times",
     "grade": "1B",
     "text": "Haematology laboratories should have access to urgent ADAMTS13 activity testing either via sample transfer to the laboratory of a regional TTP centre, or on-site.",
     "page": 2
    },
    {
     "id": "tat-2",
     "group": "Turnaround times",
     "grade": "1C",
     "text": "Local protocols should be established for urgent transfer of pre-treatment samples for ADAMTS13 activity assays in patients with suspected TTP.",
     "page": 2
    },
    {
     "id": "tat-3",
     "group": "Turnaround times",
     "grade": "1C",
     "text": "In cases of suspected TTP where an urgent ADAMTS13 activity assay is required, preliminary results should be available as soon as possible, but ideally within one hour of sample receipt by the testing laboratory for laboratories with rapid tests available, or six hours for laboratories using enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA).",
     "page": 2
    },
    {
     "id": "sample-1",
     "group": "Pre-analytical considerations",
     "grade": "1B",
     "text": "Samples should be collected into 0.109 M sodium citrate.",
     "page": 4
    },
    {
     "id": "sample-2",
     "group": "Pre-analytical considerations",
     "grade": "1B",
     "text": "For patients with a strong clinical suspicion of TTP, samples must be sent to a regional TTP centre immediately if the patient has not already been transferred.",
     "page": 4
    },
    {
     "id": "act-1",
     "group": "Testing for ADAMTS13 activity",
     "grade": "2C",
     "text": "Early confirmation with an alternative assay may be obtained in all instances when an ADAMTS13 activity <20 IU/dL is not consistent with pre-test probability and clinical assessment.",
     "page": 6
    },
    {
     "id": "act-2",
     "group": "Testing for ADAMTS13 activity",
     "grade": "1D",
     "text": "Laboratories and clinicians must have a clear understanding of the expected ranges in iTTP and cTTP at presentation of the ADAMTS13 activity assay in use.",
     "page": 6
    },
    {
     "id": "act-3",
     "group": "Testing for ADAMTS13 activity",
     "grade": "1D",
     "text": "There must be clear clinical pathways for dealing with both normal and abnormal ADAMTS13 activity results.",
     "page": 6
    },
    {
     "id": "ab-1",
     "group": "Testing for antibodies against ADAMTS13",
     "grade": "1C",
     "text": "Anti-ADAMTS13 antibody assays for clinical use should only be performed in laboratories of regional TTP centres.",
     "page": 7
    },
    {
     "id": "ab-2",
     "group": "Testing for antibodies against ADAMTS13",
     "grade": "1B",
     "text": "Anti-ADAMTS13 antibody assays must be performed when ADAMTS13 activity <10 IU/dL, within 72 h of presentation.",
     "page": 7
    },
    {
     "id": "ab-3",
     "group": "Testing for antibodies against ADAMTS13",
     "grade": "2B",
     "text": "Anti-ADAMTS13 antibody assays may be performed when there is strong clinical suspicion of TTP but ADAMTS13 activity is between 10 and 20 IU/dL.",
     "page": 7
    },
    {
     "id": "ab-4",
     "group": "Testing for antibodies against ADAMTS13",
     "grade": "2C",
     "text": "Anti-ADAMTS13 antibody assays may be repeated when ADAMTS13 activity levels remain low despite treatment for acute iTTP to guide clinical decision making for immunosuppression.",
     "page": 7
    },
    {
     "id": "ab-5",
     "group": "Testing for antibodies against ADAMTS13",
     "grade": "2B",
     "text": "Anti-ADAMTS13 antibody assays may be used to exclude acquired inhibitors for those receiving recombinant ADAMTS13.",
     "page": 7
    },
    {
     "id": "ab-6",
     "group": "Testing for antibodies against ADAMTS13",
     "grade": "2B",
     "text": "Anti-ADAMTS13 antibody assays may be performed in patients with suspected relapse of iTTP.",
     "page": 7
    },
    {
     "id": "ab-7",
     "group": "Testing for antibodies against ADAMTS13",
     "grade": "2D",
     "text": "An ELISA is recommended over non-standardised Bethesda-style inhibitor assay or mixing studies for the detection of anti-ADAMTS13 antibodies.",
     "page": 7
    },
    {
     "id": "ab-8",
     "group": "Testing for antibodies against ADAMTS13",
     "grade": "1C",
     "text": "Genomic analysis of the ADAMTS13 gene is required to confirm cTTP.",
     "page": 7
    },
    {
     "id": "ag-1",
     "group": "Testing for ADAMTS13 antigen",
     "grade": "2C",
     "text": "ADAMTS13 antigen assays are not recommended for routine clinical use.",
     "page": 7
    },
    {
     "id": "ag-2",
     "group": "Testing for ADAMTS13 antigen",
     "grade": "2C",
     "text": "ADAMTS13 antigen assays may be considered in individual patients on a case-by-case basis.",
     "page": 7
    },
    {
     "id": "ag-3",
     "group": "Testing for ADAMTS13 antigen",
     "grade": "1C",
     "text": "ADAMTS13 antigen assays for clinical use should only be performed in laboratories of regional TTP centres.",
     "page": 7
    },
    {
     "id": "conf-1",
     "group": "ADAMTS13 conformation (open/closed index) assay",
     "grade": "2C",
     "text": "ADAMTS13 conformation assays are not currently recommended for routine clinical use.",
     "page": 8
    },
    {
     "id": "conf-2",
     "group": "ADAMTS13 conformation (open/closed index) assay",
     "grade": "1C",
     "text": "ADAMTS13 conformation assays for clinical use should only be performed in laboratories of regional TTP centres.",
     "page": 8
    },
    {
     "id": "mon-1",
     "group": "Laboratory monitoring in recovery and relapse",
     "grade": "1C",
     "text": "ADAMTS13 activity assay differences indicate that for monitoring, and identification of remission and relapse, the same analytical method should be used in any single patient to retain sensitivity for clinically significant changes.",
     "page": 8
    },
    {
     "id": "mon-2",
     "group": "Laboratory monitoring in recovery and relapse",
     "grade": "2B",
     "text": "Laboratories may consider confirmation on a second platform when ADAMTS13 activity is unexpectedly low, or results appear discordant with the clinical picture.",
     "page": 8
    }
   ],
   "topicIds": [
    "ttp-recognition",
    "ttp-samples",
    "ttp-adamts13-activity",
    "ttp-antibodies",
    "ttp-antigen-conformation",
    "ttp-monitoring"
   ],
